WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.179
Episode three: fields and rules.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.205
Every question in the form is a field object.

3
00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:08.475
The type in the JSON picks its class, using a registry:

4
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.042
a plain object that maps a name to the code that handles it.

5
00:00:12.042 --> 00:00:15.193
To add a new kind of question, you add one line here.

6
00:00:15.545 --> 00:00:21.507
If the CRM sends a type nobody knows, the form shows a plain text box and warns in the console.

7
00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:23.704
A typo never breaks the whole page.

8
00:00:24.053 --> 00:00:26.899
All field classes share one parent: BaseField.

9
00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:30.488
Its render method fixes the order of the parts: the label,

10
00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:33.396
the help text, the input, and the photo button.

11
00:00:33.396 --> 00:00:37.047
Each field type replaces only the parts that are different.

12
00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:41.294
Here is a complete field type: the Yes / No / N/A buttons.

13
00:00:41.294 --> 00:00:43.443
Each button just calls setValue.

14
00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.592
It never changes its own colour.

15
00:00:45.944 --> 00:00:48.766
Its refresh method does that, after every change,

16
00:00:48.766 --> 00:00:52.222
by checking which answer is selected and what its status is.

17
00:00:52.574 --> 00:00:55.236
So how does the form decide that No is red?

18
00:00:55.236 --> 00:00:58.394
A question can have an evaluation rule in the JSON.

19
00:00:58.394 --> 00:01:00.437
The rule’s type picks a function.

20
00:01:00.437 --> 00:01:05.267
expectedValue, for example, passes when the answer equals the expected answer.

21
00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:09.561
Then small functions, with no page code at all, roll the answers up.

22
00:01:09.561 --> 00:01:11.590
A unit is red if any answer is red,

23
00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:15.184
and green only when everything is answered and nothing failed.

24
00:01:15.535 --> 00:01:17.474
Let’s see the three outcomes.

25
00:01:17.474 --> 00:01:18.210
Yes passes.

26
00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.414
No is flagged.

27
00:01:19.809 --> 00:01:22.294
And N/A is a valid answer, with no colour.

28
00:01:22.294 --> 00:01:25.075
All three count towards the section’s progress.

29
00:01:25.427 --> 00:01:28.174
Next: sections, widgets and buttons.
